{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A99hqbGVu53dbHZgvKuyHR","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Is the sandwich `degeneracy ≤ pathwidth ≤ bandwidth` a theorem in the Lean development?\n\nThe Lean side is `lean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean`: it defines degeneracy\n(both the Lick–White subgraph form and the elimination-ordering form) and\nbandwidth over the repository's graph definitions, proves\n`degeneracy ≤ vertexSeparation` and `vertexSeparation ≤ bandwidth`, and carries\nthem to pathwidth through `VSEquivPW` (Kinnersley), and proves the two\ndegeneracy forms equal by the greedy elimination ordering. Since loop0004\nitem 12 (2026-09-28) it also proves `treewidth ≤ pathwidth` (every path\ndecomposition is a tree decomposition on the path graph, which the file proves\nis a tree) and the pathwidth branch lemma of Fellows & Langston (1987) /\nKinnersley (1992) — three disjoint connected branches of pathwidth ≥ k attached\nto one vertex force pathwidth ≥ k + 1 — together with a Lean proof that the\nstatement previously carried with `sorry`, which lacked the attachment and\nconnectivity hypotheses, was false. Since item 13 (2026-09-28) it also proves\nthe *separator* form, Lemma A of `reports/ml_nature.md` §38: the cut vertex\nreplaced by connectors — connected subsets of a separator `S`, one per pair of\nbranches — with the cut-vertex lemma re-derived as the case `S = {v}`. One\nstatement stands with `sorry`: item 09's fitted conjecture, left as a statement\non purpose.\n\nThis module answers the two questions a proof about a definition leaves open:\n\n1. **Do the Lean definitions compute the textbook quantities?**\n   `degeneracy_subsets`, `ordering_degeneracy`, `bandwidth` and\n   `vertex_separation` transcribe the Lean definitions literally (brute force\n   over subsets and layouts) and are compared, on every graph on at most\n   `--max-n` vertices (default 5, 1,044 graphs), with networkx's core number,\n   with the exact pathwidth solver, and with each other (the proved equality\n   `orderingDegeneracy = degeneracy` is checked exhaustively at that size as\n   a guard on the two definitions).\n2. **Which theorems rest on which axioms?** `--stage lean` runs `lake build`\n   and `#print axioms` on every named theorem, recording whether `sorryAx`\n   appears. The proved theorems must not use it; the stated ones must.\n\nIt also recounts the corpus check the plan cites (`g_degeneracy + 1 ≤ optimum\n≤ bw_rcm + 1` on `learning/data/instances.csv`), so that the number in the\nreport is regenerated rather than copied.\n\nRun::\n\n    python -m learning.sandwich                       # everything, ~1 min\n    python -m learning.sandwich --stage brute --max-n 5\n    python -m learning.sandwich --stage lean\n    python -m learning.sandwich --stage corpus\n\nWrites `reports/sandwich_tables.md`. Nothing here is a bound, a solver change,\nor written to `solutions/`.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport itertools\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport networkx as nx\n    (Lemma 5 of §6.2, proved in Lean as the pair of inequalities); returns the number of `N`.\"\"\"\n    for N in range(max_n + 1):\n        assert tree_bound_lean(N) == tree_bound_least(N), N\n    return max_n + 1\n\n\ndef _md(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> str:\n    return frame.to_markdown(index=False)\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])\n    ap.add_argument(\"--stage\", choices=[\"all\", \"brute\", \"lean\", \"corpus\", \"forest\"], default=\"all\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=5)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=Path, default=TABLES)\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n\n    sections = [\"# The sandwich in Lean: tables\", \"\",\n                \"Regenerate: `python -m learning.sandwich`. Every table below is \"\n                \"written by that command; `reports/ml_nature.md` §26 quotes them.\", \"\"]\n    ok = True\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"brute\"):\n        t0 = time.time()\n        frame = brute_force(args.max_n)\n        summary = brute_summary(frame)\n        sections += [f\"## Brute force over every labelled graph on 1–{args.max_n} vertices\",\n                     \"\", f\"{len(frame)} graphs in {time.time() - t0:.1f} s. \"\n                     \"Each column counts graphs where the statement holds.\", \"\",\n                     _md(summary), \"\"]\n        bad = frame[(frame.degeneracy != frame.core_number)\n                    | (frame.degeneracy != frame.ordering_degeneracy)\n                    | (frame.vertex_separation != frame.pathwidth_solver)\n                    | (frame.degeneracy > frame.vertex_separation)\n                    | (frame.vertex_separation > frame.bandwidth)]\n        ok &= bad.empty\n        print(summary.to_string(index=False))\n        print(f\"brute force: {len(frame)} graphs, {len(bad)} violations\")\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"corpus\"):\n        corpus = corpus_check()\n        sections += [\"## The corpus (`learning/data/instances.csv`)\", \"\",\n                     \"`g_degeneracy` is networkx's core number (the Lick–White form \"\n                     \"formalised as `degeneracy`); `bw_rcm` is the bandwidth of the \"\n                     \"reverse Cuthill–McKee layout (`bandwidthOfLayout`, one layout, \"\n                     \"so `pathwidth_le_bandwidthOfLayout` is the theorem it checks).\", \"\",\n                     _md(corpus), \"\"]\n        total = corpus[corpus.band == \"all\"].iloc[0]\n        ok &= total[\"degeneracy+1 ≤ optimum\"] == total.instances == total[\"optimum ≤ bw_rcm+1\"]\n        print(corpus.to_string(index=False))\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"forest\"):\n        forest = forest_cover_check()\n        n_ident = tree_bound_identity_check()\n        sections += [\"## `ForestCover.lean` against item 03's record \"\n                     \"(`reports/scratch/forest_check/record_check.csv`)\", \"\",\n                     \"(L2) `pw(G_M) + 1 ≤ (pw(B) + 1) ω` on the rows where both pathwidths are \"\n                     \"exact; (L4) `pw(G_M) + 1 ≤ ω (tb(n + m) + 1)` on every row with `pw(G_M)` \"\n                     \"exact (every record row's incidence graph is a forest); `tb` is \"\n                     \"`treeBoundInv` as Lean defines it, equal to the least `k` with \"\n                     f\"`N ≤ treeBound k` for every `N < {n_ident}` (checked).\", \"\",\n                     _md(forest), \"\"]\n        total = forest[forest.family == \"all\"].iloc[0]\n        ok &= total[\"L2 violations\"] == 0 and total[\"L4 violations\"] == 0\n        print(forest.to_string(index=False))\n        print(f\"forest cover: {total['rows']} rows, {total['L2 violations']} L2 violations, \"\n              f\"{total['L4 violations']} L4 violations; tb identity on {n_ident} values\")\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"lean\"):\n        if not lake_available():\n            sections += [\"## Lean\", \"\", \"`lake` not available; axiom check skipped.\", \"\"]\n            print(\"lake not available\")\n        else:\n            t0 = time.time()\n            built, tail = lake_build()\n            axioms = print_axioms()\n            verdict, problems = axioms_verdict(axioms)\n            ok &= built and verdict\n            sections += [\"## Lean: `lake build` and `#print axioms`\", \"\",\n                         f\"`lake build`: {'passed' if built else 'FAILED'} in \"\n                         f\"{time.time() - t0:.0f} s.\", \"\",\n                         _md(axioms.drop(columns=[\"found\"])), \"\",\n                         \"Verdict: \" + (\"every proved theorem is free of `sorryAx`, every \"\n                                        \"stated one carries it.\" if verdict\n                                        else \"; \".join(problems)), \"\"]\n            print(axioms.to_string(index=False))\n            print(\"lake build:\", \"ok\" if built else \"FAILED\", \"| axioms:\",\n                  \"ok\" if verdict else problems)\n            if not built:\n                print(tail)\n\n    args.out.write_text(\"\\n\".join(sections))\n    print(f\"wrote {args.out}\")\n    return 0 if ok else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\nleanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2\nimport Lake\nopen Lake DSL\n\npackage MOSPFormalization where\n  leanOptions := #[\n    ⟨`autoImplicit, false⟩\n  ]\n\n@[default_target]\nlean_lib MOSPFormalization where\n  srcDir := \".\"\n\nrequire \"leanprover-community\" / \"mathlib\" @ git \"master\"\n  pattern meets both sides, `∏_j avoidCount n |A| |R| (s j)` of them.\n* `card_coversOfPathwidthLe_le` — **the first-moment count**: for `k < n`,\n  `#{S ∈ covers s : pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k} ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j)`.\n* `prob_coversOfPathwidthLe_le` — **the probability form**, over `ℝ`:\n  `#{…} / ∏_j n.choose (s j) ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j (avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j) / n.choose (s j))`.\n* `coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe` — with `m ≥ 1` and every\n  `s j ≥ 1` (so some customer requires some pattern), `mospValue ≤ k + 1` and\n  `pathwidth ≤ k` cut out the same covers (`mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`);\n  `card_coversOfMospValueLe_le`, `prob_coversOfMospValueLe_le` — **the MOSP\n  reading** of both bounds.\n\nNo `sorry`; axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only.\n-/\n\nimport MOSPFormalization.FirstMoment\nimport MOSPFormalization.MOSPGraph\nimport Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators\n\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization\n\nopen Finset\n\nvariable {C : Type*} [Fintype C] [DecidableEq C] {m : ℕ}\n\n/-! ### Covers and their instances -/\n\n/-- The clique covers with size vector `s`: one `s j`-subset of the customers per\npattern `j`. -/\ndef covers (s : Fin m → ℕ) : Finset (Fin m → Finset C) :=\n    (coverInstance S).requires c j ↔ c ∈ S j := Iff.rfl\n\n/-- The graph of a cover: the MOSP graph of its instance, customers adjacent iff\nsome pattern contains both. -/\nabbrev coverGraph (S : Fin m → Finset C) : SimpleGraph C :=\n  (coverInstance S).mospGraph\n\ntheorem coverGraph_adj {S : Fin m → Finset C} {u v : C} :\n    (coverGraph S).Adj u v ↔ u ≠ v ∧ ∃ j, u ∈ S j ∧ v ∈ S j := Iff.rfl\n\n/-! ### Empty pairs of a cover -/\n\n/-- For disjoint `A`, `R`: `(A, R)` is an empty pair of the cover's graph iff no\npattern meets both sides. -/\ntheorem isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff {S : Fin m → Finset C} {A R : Finset C}\n    (hAR : Disjoint A R) :\n    IsEmptyPair (coverGraph S) A R ↔ ∀ j, Disjoint (S j) A ∨ Disjoint (S j) R := by\n  constructor\n  · intro h j\n    by_contra hc\n    rw [not_or, Finset.not_disjoint_iff, Finset.not_disjoint_iff] at hc\n    obtain ⟨⟨a, haS, haA⟩, ⟨r, hrS, hrR⟩⟩ := hc\n    exact h a haA r hrR\n      ⟨fun hne => Finset.disjoint_left.1 hAR haA (hne ▸ hrR), j, haS, hrS⟩\n  · intro h a ha r hr hadj\n    obtain ⟨_, j, haS, hrS⟩ := hadj\n    rcases h j with hj | hj\n    · exact Finset.disjoint_left.1 hj haS ha\n    · exact Finset.disjoint_left.1 hj hrS hr\n\n/-! ### Counting the patterns that avoid a side -/\n\n/-- The `s`-subsets of the customers disjoint from `A`: `(n − |A|).choose s` of them. -/\ntheorem card_powersetCard_filter_disjoint (A : Finset C) (s : ℕ) :\n    (((univ : Finset C).powersetCard s).filter (fun T => Disjoint T A)).card =\n      (Fintype.card C - A.card).choose s := by\n\n/-! ### The union bound -/\n\n/-- The covers with size vector `s` whose graph has pathwidth at most `k`. -/\nnoncomputable def coversOfPathwidthLe (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) : Finset (Fin m → Finset C) := by\n  classical exact (covers s).filter (fun S => pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k)\n\ntheorem mem_coversOfPathwidthLe {s : Fin m → ℕ} {k : ℕ} {S : Fin m → Finset C} :\n    S ∈ coversOfPathwidthLe s k ↔ S ∈ covers s ∧ pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k := by\n  simp [coversOfPathwidthLe]\n\n/-- Every cover of pathwidth `≤ k < n` lies in the set of some pair `(A, R)` with\n`|A| = t`, `|R| = t − 1`, `t = (n − k + 1) / 2`: by `exists_empty_pair`, shrinking\nthe pair, and `isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff`. -/\ntheorem mem_biUnion_emptyPairCovers {s : Fin m → ℕ} {k : ℕ} (hk : k < Fintype.card C)\n    {S : Fin m → Finset C} (hS : S ∈ covers s) (hpw : pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k) :\n    S ∈ (emptyPairIndices ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)).biUnion\n      (fun p => emptyPairCovers s p.1 p.2) := by\n  obtain ⟨A, R, hAR, hedge, hA, hR⟩ := exists_empty_pair (coverGraph S) (by omega)\n  obtain ⟨A', hA'A, hA'⟩ := Finset.exists_subset_card_eq\n    (s := A) (n := (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) (by omega)\n  obtain ⟨R', hR'R, hR'⟩ := Finset.exists_subset_card_eq\n    (s := R) (n := (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (by omega)\n  have hAR' : Disjoint A' R' :=\n    Finset.disjoint_of_subset_left hA'A (Finset.disjoint_of_subset_right hR'R hAR)\n  rw [mem_biUnion]\n  refine ⟨⟨A', R'⟩, mem_emptyPairIndices.2 ⟨hA', ?_, hR'⟩, ?_⟩\n  · intro r hr\n    rw [mem_sdiff]\n    exact ⟨mem_univ r, fun hrA => Finset.disjoint_left.1 hAR' hrA hr⟩\n  · rw [mem_emptyPairCovers]\n    refine ⟨mem_covers.1 hS, ?_⟩\n    exact (isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff hAR').1\n      (fun a ha r hr => hedge a (hA'A ha) r (hR'R hr))\n\n/-- **The first-moment count on clique covers.** For `k < n = |C|` and\n`t = (n − k + 1) / 2`,\n`#{S ∈ covers s : pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k} ≤\n  n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j)`. -/\ntheorem card_coversOfPathwidthLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    (coversOfPathwidthLe (C := C) s k).card ≤\n      (Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) *\n        ∏ j, avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) := by\n  classical\n  set t := (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 with ht\n  calc (coversOfPathwidthLe (C := C) s k).card\n      ≤ ((emptyPairIndices t).biUnion (fun p => emptyPairCovers s p.1 p.2)).card :=\n        card_le_card (fun S hS => by\n          obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := mem_coversOfPathwidthLe.1 hS\n          exact mem_biUnion_emptyPairCovers hk h1 h2)\n    _ ≤ (emptyPairIndices (V := C) t).card *\n          ∏ j, avoidCount (Fintype.card C) t (t - 1) (s j) := by\n        refine card_biUnion_le_card_mul _ _ _ (fun p hp => ?_)\n        obtain ⟨hA, _, hR⟩ := mem_emptyPairIndices.1 hp\n        rw [card_emptyPairCovers s (disjoint_of_mem_emptyPairIndices hp), hA, hR]\n    _ = _ := by rw [card_emptyPairIndices]\n\n/-! ### The probability form -/\n\n/-- **The first-moment bound on random clique covers**, over `ℝ`: with every\ncover of size vector `s` equally likely, `k < n = |C|`, `t = (n − k + 1) / 2`,\n`q(s) = avoidCount n t (t − 1) s / n.choose s`,\n`P(pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k) ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j q(s j)`,\nthe inequality of `reports/scratch/clique_cover_moment/finite_bound_cs.py`. -/\ntheorem prob_coversOfPathwidthLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    ((coversOfPathwidthLe (C := C) s k).card : ℝ) /\n        ∏ j, ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ) ≤\n      (((Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) : ℕ) : ℝ) *\n        ∏ j, ((avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) : ℝ) /\n            ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ)) := by\n/-! ### The MOSP reading -/\n\n/-- The covers with size vector `s` whose instance has MOSP value at most `k`. -/\nnoncomputable def coversOfMospValueLe (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) : Finset (Fin m → Finset C) := by\n  classical exact (covers s).filter (fun S => (coverInstance S).mospValue ≤ k)\n\ntheorem mem_coversOfMospValueLe {s : Fin m → ℕ} {k : ℕ} {S : Fin m → Finset C} :\n    S ∈ coversOfMospValueLe s k ↔ S ∈ covers s ∧ (coverInstance S).mospValue ≤ k := by\n  simp [coversOfMospValueLe]\n\n/-- With at least one pattern and no empty pattern, some customer requires some\npattern in every cover, the hypothesis of `mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`. -/\ntheorem exists_requires_of_mem_covers {s : Fin m → ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j)\n    {S : Fin m → Finset C} (hS : S ∈ covers s) :\n    ∃ c p, (coverInstance S).requires c p := by\n  have hcard : 0 < (S ⟨0, hm⟩).card := by\n    rw [mem_covers.1 hS ⟨0, hm⟩]\n    exact hs _\n  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Finset.card_pos.1 hcard\n  exact ⟨c, ⟨0, hm⟩, hc⟩\n\n/-- `mospValue ≤ k + 1` and `pathwidth ≤ k` cut out the same covers, by Yanasse's\nequality, when `m ≥ 1` and every pattern is nonempty. -/\ntheorem coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe {s : Fin m → ℕ} (hm : 0 < m)\n    (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j) (k : ℕ) :\n    coversOfMospValueLe (C := C) s (k + 1) = coversOfPathwidthLe s k := by\n  ext S\n  rw [mem_coversOfMospValueLe, mem_coversOfPathwidthLe]\n  constructor\n  · rintro ⟨hS, h⟩\n    refine ⟨hS, ?_⟩\n    rw [(coverInstance S).mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one\n      (exists_requires_of_mem_covers hm hs hS)] at h\n    exact Nat.le_of_add_le_add_right h\n  · rintro ⟨hS, h⟩\n    refine ⟨hS, ?_⟩\n    rw [(coverInstance S).mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one\n      (exists_requires_of_mem_covers hm hs hS)]\n    exact Nat.add_le_add_right h 1\n\n/-- **The first-moment count, MOSP reading.** With `m ≥ 1`, every `s j ≥ 1` and\n`k < n = |C|`, `t = (n − k + 1) / 2`,\n`#{S ∈ covers s : mospValue (coverInstance S) ≤ k + 1} ≤\n  n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j)`. -/\ntheorem card_coversOfMospValueLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (hm : 0 < m) (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j)\n    (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    (coversOfMospValueLe (C := C) s (k + 1)).card ≤\n      (Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) *\n        ∏ j, avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) := by\n  rw [coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe hm hs]\n  exact card_coversOfPathwidthLe_le s k hk\n\n/-- **The first-moment bound, MOSP reading**, over `ℝ`: the probability that a\nuniformly random cover of size vector `s` has MOSP value at most `k + 1`. -/\ntheorem prob_coversOfMospValueLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (hm : 0 < m) (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j)\n    (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    ((coversOfMospValueLe (C := C) s (k + 1)).card : ℝ) /\n        ∏ j, ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ) ≤\n      (((Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) : ℕ) : ℝ) *\n        ∏ j, ((avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) : ℝ) /\n            ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ)) := by\n  rw [coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe hm hs]\n  exact prob_coversOfPathwidthLe_le s k hk\n\nend MOSPFormalization","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6993792e-f360-4099-9cf6-566b61424ef2","uuid":"af2f1436-f451-4a23-9d6c-496f883bc4b4","timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:52:52.900Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Is the sandwich `degeneracy ≤ pathwidth ≤ bandwidth` a theorem in the Lean development?\n\nThe Lean side is `lean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean`: it defines degeneracy\n(both the Lick–White subgraph form and the elimination-ordering form) and\nbandwidth over the repository's graph definitions, proves\n`degeneracy ≤ vertexSeparation` and `vertexSeparation ≤ bandwidth`, and carries\nthem to pathwidth through `VSEquivPW` (Kinnersley), and proves the two\ndegeneracy forms equal by the greedy elimination ordering. Since loop0004\nitem 12 (2026-09-28) it also proves `treewidth ≤ pathwidth` (every path\ndecomposition is a tree decomposition on the path graph, which the file proves\nis a tree) and the pathwidth branch lemma of Fellows & Langston (1987) /\nKinnersley (1992) — three disjoint connected branches of pathwidth ≥ k attached\nto one vertex force pathwidth ≥ k + 1 — together with a Lean proof that the\nstatement previously carried with `sorry`, which lacked the attachment and\nconnectivity hypotheses, was false. Since item 13 (2026-09-28) it also proves\nthe *separator* form, Lemma A of `reports/ml_nature.md` §38: the cut vertex\nreplaced by connectors — connected subsets of a separator `S`, one per pair of\nbranches — with the cut-vertex lemma re-derived as the case `S = {v}`. One\nstatement stands with `sorry`: item 09's fitted conjecture, left as a statement\non purpose.\n\nThis module answers the two questions a proof about a definition leaves open:\n\n1. **Do the Lean definitions compute the textbook quantities?**\n   `degeneracy_subsets`, `ordering_degeneracy`, `bandwidth` and\n   `vertex_separation` transcribe the Lean definitions literally (brute force\n   over subsets and layouts) and are compared, on every graph on at most\n   `--max-n` vertices (default 5, 1,044 graphs), with networkx's core number,\n   with the exact pathwidth solver, and with each other (the proved equality\n   `orderingDegeneracy = degeneracy` is checked exhaustively at that size as\n   a guard on the two definitions).\n2. **Which theorems rest on which axioms?** `--stage lean` runs `lake build`\n   and `#print axioms` on every named theorem, recording whether `sorryAx`\n   appears. The proved theorems must not use it; the stated ones must.\n\nIt also recounts the corpus check the plan cites (`g_degeneracy + 1 ≤ optimum\n≤ bw_rcm + 1` on `learning/data/instances.csv`), so that the number in the\nreport is regenerated rather than copied.\n\nRun::\n\n    python -m learning.sandwich                       # everything, ~1 min\n    python -m learning.sandwich --stage brute --max-n 5\n    python -m learning.sandwich --stage lean\n    python -m learning.sandwich --stage corpus\n\nWrites `reports/sandwich_tables.md`. Nothing here is a bound, a solver change,\nor written to `solutions/`.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport itertools\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport networkx as nx\n    (Lemma 5 of §6.2, proved in Lean as the pair of inequalities); returns the number of `N`.\"\"\"\n    for N in range(max_n + 1):\n        assert tree_bound_lean(N) == tree_bound_least(N), N\n    return max_n + 1\n\n\ndef _md(frame: pd.DataFrame) -> str:\n    return frame.to_markdown(index=False)\n\n\ndef main(argv=None) -> int:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])\n    ap.add_argument(\"--stage\", choices=[\"all\", \"brute\", \"lean\", \"corpus\", \"forest\"], default=\"all\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=5)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=Path, default=TABLES)\n    args = ap.parse_args(argv)\n\n    sections = [\"# The sandwich in Lean: tables\", \"\",\n                \"Regenerate: `python -m learning.sandwich`. Every table below is \"\n                \"written by that command; `reports/ml_nature.md` §26 quotes them.\", \"\"]\n    ok = True\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"brute\"):\n        t0 = time.time()\n        frame = brute_force(args.max_n)\n        summary = brute_summary(frame)\n        sections += [f\"## Brute force over every labelled graph on 1–{args.max_n} vertices\",\n                     \"\", f\"{len(frame)} graphs in {time.time() - t0:.1f} s. \"\n                     \"Each column counts graphs where the statement holds.\", \"\",\n                     _md(summary), \"\"]\n        bad = frame[(frame.degeneracy != frame.core_number)\n                    | (frame.degeneracy != frame.ordering_degeneracy)\n                    | (frame.vertex_separation != frame.pathwidth_solver)\n                    | (frame.degeneracy > frame.vertex_separation)\n                    | (frame.vertex_separation > frame.bandwidth)]\n        ok &= bad.empty\n        print(summary.to_string(index=False))\n        print(f\"brute force: {len(frame)} graphs, {len(bad)} violations\")\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"corpus\"):\n        corpus = corpus_check()\n        sections += [\"## The corpus (`learning/data/instances.csv`)\", \"\",\n                     \"`g_degeneracy` is networkx's core number (the Lick–White form \"\n                     \"formalised as `degeneracy`); `bw_rcm` is the bandwidth of the \"\n                     \"reverse Cuthill–McKee layout (`bandwidthOfLayout`, one layout, \"\n                     \"so `pathwidth_le_bandwidthOfLayout` is the theorem it checks).\", \"\",\n                     _md(corpus), \"\"]\n        total = corpus[corpus.band == \"all\"].iloc[0]\n        ok &= total[\"degeneracy+1 ≤ optimum\"] == total.instances == total[\"optimum ≤ bw_rcm+1\"]\n        print(corpus.to_string(index=False))\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"forest\"):\n        forest = forest_cover_check()\n        n_ident = tree_bound_identity_check()\n        sections += [\"## `ForestCover.lean` against item 03's record \"\n                     \"(`reports/scratch/forest_check/record_check.csv`)\", \"\",\n                     \"(L2) `pw(G_M) + 1 ≤ (pw(B) + 1) ω` on the rows where both pathwidths are \"\n                     \"exact; (L4) `pw(G_M) + 1 ≤ ω (tb(n + m) + 1)` on every row with `pw(G_M)` \"\n                     \"exact (every record row's incidence graph is a forest); `tb` is \"\n                     \"`treeBoundInv` as Lean defines it, equal to the least `k` with \"\n                     f\"`N ≤ treeBound k` for every `N < {n_ident}` (checked).\", \"\",\n                     _md(forest), \"\"]\n        total = forest[forest.family == \"all\"].iloc[0]\n        ok &= total[\"L2 violations\"] == 0 and total[\"L4 violations\"] == 0\n        print(forest.to_string(index=False))\n        print(f\"forest cover: {total['rows']} rows, {total['L2 violations']} L2 violations, \"\n              f\"{total['L4 violations']} L4 violations; tb identity on {n_ident} values\")\n\n    if args.stage in (\"all\", \"lean\"):\n        if not lake_available():\n            sections += [\"## Lean\", \"\", \"`lake` not available; axiom check skipped.\", \"\"]\n            print(\"lake not available\")\n        else:\n            t0 = time.time()\n            built, tail = lake_build()\n            axioms = print_axioms()\n            verdict, problems = axioms_verdict(axioms)\n            ok &= built and verdict\n            sections += [\"## Lean: `lake build` and `#print axioms`\", \"\",\n                         f\"`lake build`: {'passed' if built else 'FAILED'} in \"\n                         f\"{time.time() - t0:.0f} s.\", \"\",\n                         _md(axioms.drop(columns=[\"found\"])), \"\",\n                         \"Verdict: \" + (\"every proved theorem is free of `sorryAx`, every \"\n                                        \"stated one carries it.\" if verdict\n                                        else \"; \".join(problems)), \"\"]\n            print(axioms.to_string(index=False))\n            print(\"lake build:\", \"ok\" if built else \"FAILED\", \"| axioms:\",\n                  \"ok\" if verdict else problems)\n            if not built:\n                print(tail)\n\n    args.out.write_text(\"\\n\".join(sections))\n    print(f\"wrote {args.out}\")\n    return 0 if ok else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\nleanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2\nimport Lake\nopen Lake DSL\n\npackage MOSPFormalization where\n  leanOptions := #[\n    ⟨`autoImplicit, false⟩\n  ]\n\n@[default_target]\nlean_lib MOSPFormalization where\n  srcDir := \".\"\n\nrequire \"leanprover-community\" / \"mathlib\" @ git \"master\"\n  pattern meets both sides, `∏_j avoidCount n |A| |R| (s j)` of them.\n* `card_coversOfPathwidthLe_le` — **the first-moment count**: for `k < n`,\n  `#{S ∈ covers s : pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k} ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j)`.\n* `prob_coversOfPathwidthLe_le` — **the probability form**, over `ℝ`:\n  `#{…} / ∏_j n.choose (s j) ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j (avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j) / n.choose (s j))`.\n* `coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe` — with `m ≥ 1` and every\n  `s j ≥ 1` (so some customer requires some pattern), `mospValue ≤ k + 1` and\n  `pathwidth ≤ k` cut out the same covers (`mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`);\n  `card_coversOfMospValueLe_le`, `prob_coversOfMospValueLe_le` — **the MOSP\n  reading** of both bounds.\n\nNo `sorry`; axioms `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` only.\n-/\n\nimport MOSPFormalization.FirstMoment\nimport MOSPFormalization.MOSPGraph\nimport Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators\n\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization\n\nopen Finset\n\nvariable {C : Type*} [Fintype C] [DecidableEq C] {m : ℕ}\n\n/-! ### Covers and their instances -/\n\n/-- The clique covers with size vector `s`: one `s j`-subset of the customers per\npattern `j`. -/\ndef covers (s : Fin m → ℕ) : Finset (Fin m → Finset C) :=\n    (coverInstance S).requires c j ↔ c ∈ S j := Iff.rfl\n\n/-- The graph of a cover: the MOSP graph of its instance, customers adjacent iff\nsome pattern contains both. -/\nabbrev coverGraph (S : Fin m → Finset C) : SimpleGraph C :=\n  (coverInstance S).mospGraph\n\ntheorem coverGraph_adj {S : Fin m → Finset C} {u v : C} :\n    (coverGraph S).Adj u v ↔ u ≠ v ∧ ∃ j, u ∈ S j ∧ v ∈ S j := Iff.rfl\n\n/-! ### Empty pairs of a cover -/\n\n/-- For disjoint `A`, `R`: `(A, R)` is an empty pair of the cover's graph iff no\npattern meets both sides. -/\ntheorem isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff {S : Fin m → Finset C} {A R : Finset C}\n    (hAR : Disjoint A R) :\n    IsEmptyPair (coverGraph S) A R ↔ ∀ j, Disjoint (S j) A ∨ Disjoint (S j) R := by\n  constructor\n  · intro h j\n    by_contra hc\n    rw [not_or, Finset.not_disjoint_iff, Finset.not_disjoint_iff] at hc\n    obtain ⟨⟨a, haS, haA⟩, ⟨r, hrS, hrR⟩⟩ := hc\n    exact h a haA r hrR\n      ⟨fun hne => Finset.disjoint_left.1 hAR haA (hne ▸ hrR), j, haS, hrS⟩\n  · intro h a ha r hr hadj\n    obtain ⟨_, j, haS, hrS⟩ := hadj\n    rcases h j with hj | hj\n    · exact Finset.disjoint_left.1 hj haS ha\n    · exact Finset.disjoint_left.1 hj hrS hr\n\n/-! ### Counting the patterns that avoid a side -/\n\n/-- The `s`-subsets of the customers disjoint from `A`: `(n − |A|).choose s` of them. -/\ntheorem card_powersetCard_filter_disjoint (A : Finset C) (s : ℕ) :\n    (((univ : Finset C).powersetCard s).filter (fun T => Disjoint T A)).card =\n      (Fintype.card C - A.card).choose s := by\n\n/-! ### The union bound -/\n\n/-- The covers with size vector `s` whose graph has pathwidth at most `k`. -/\nnoncomputable def coversOfPathwidthLe (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) : Finset (Fin m → Finset C) := by\n  classical exact (covers s).filter (fun S => pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k)\n\ntheorem mem_coversOfPathwidthLe {s : Fin m → ℕ} {k : ℕ} {S : Fin m → Finset C} :\n    S ∈ coversOfPathwidthLe s k ↔ S ∈ covers s ∧ pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k := by\n  simp [coversOfPathwidthLe]\n\n/-- Every cover of pathwidth `≤ k < n` lies in the set of some pair `(A, R)` with\n`|A| = t`, `|R| = t − 1`, `t = (n − k + 1) / 2`: by `exists_empty_pair`, shrinking\nthe pair, and `isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff`. -/\ntheorem mem_biUnion_emptyPairCovers {s : Fin m → ℕ} {k : ℕ} (hk : k < Fintype.card C)\n    {S : Fin m → Finset C} (hS : S ∈ covers s) (hpw : pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k) :\n    S ∈ (emptyPairIndices ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)).biUnion\n      (fun p => emptyPairCovers s p.1 p.2) := by\n  obtain ⟨A, R, hAR, hedge, hA, hR⟩ := exists_empty_pair (coverGraph S) (by omega)\n  obtain ⟨A', hA'A, hA'⟩ := Finset.exists_subset_card_eq\n    (s := A) (n := (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) (by omega)\n  obtain ⟨R', hR'R, hR'⟩ := Finset.exists_subset_card_eq\n    (s := R) (n := (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (by omega)\n  have hAR' : Disjoint A' R' :=\n    Finset.disjoint_of_subset_left hA'A (Finset.disjoint_of_subset_right hR'R hAR)\n  rw [mem_biUnion]\n  refine ⟨⟨A', R'⟩, mem_emptyPairIndices.2 ⟨hA', ?_, hR'⟩, ?_⟩\n  · intro r hr\n    rw [mem_sdiff]\n    exact ⟨mem_univ r, fun hrA => Finset.disjoint_left.1 hAR' hrA hr⟩\n  · rw [mem_emptyPairCovers]\n    refine ⟨mem_covers.1 hS, ?_⟩\n    exact (isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff hAR').1\n      (fun a ha r hr => hedge a (hA'A ha) r (hR'R hr))\n\n/-- **The first-moment count on clique covers.** For `k < n = |C|` and\n`t = (n − k + 1) / 2`,\n`#{S ∈ covers s : pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k} ≤\n  n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j)`. -/\ntheorem card_coversOfPathwidthLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    (coversOfPathwidthLe (C := C) s k).card ≤\n      (Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) *\n        ∏ j, avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) := by\n  classical\n  set t := (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 with ht\n  calc (coversOfPathwidthLe (C := C) s k).card\n      ≤ ((emptyPairIndices t).biUnion (fun p => emptyPairCovers s p.1 p.2)).card :=\n        card_le_card (fun S hS => by\n          obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := mem_coversOfPathwidthLe.1 hS\n          exact mem_biUnion_emptyPairCovers hk h1 h2)\n    _ ≤ (emptyPairIndices (V := C) t).card *\n          ∏ j, avoidCount (Fintype.card C) t (t - 1) (s j) := by\n        refine card_biUnion_le_card_mul _ _ _ (fun p hp => ?_)\n        obtain ⟨hA, _, hR⟩ := mem_emptyPairIndices.1 hp\n        rw [card_emptyPairCovers s (disjoint_of_mem_emptyPairIndices hp), hA, hR]\n    _ = _ := by rw [card_emptyPairIndices]\n\n/-! ### The probability form -/\n\n/-- **The first-moment bound on random clique covers**, over `ℝ`: with every\ncover of size vector `s` equally likely, `k < n = |C|`, `t = (n − k + 1) / 2`,\n`q(s) = avoidCount n t (t − 1) s / n.choose s`,\n`P(pathwidth (coverGraph S) ≤ k) ≤ n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j q(s j)`,\nthe inequality of `reports/scratch/clique_cover_moment/finite_bound_cs.py`. -/\ntheorem prob_coversOfPathwidthLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    ((coversOfPathwidthLe (C := C) s k).card : ℝ) /\n        ∏ j, ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ) ≤\n      (((Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) : ℕ) : ℝ) *\n        ∏ j, ((avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) : ℝ) /\n            ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ)) := by\n/-! ### The MOSP reading -/\n\n/-- The covers with size vector `s` whose instance has MOSP value at most `k`. -/\nnoncomputable def coversOfMospValueLe (s : Fin m → ℕ) (k : ℕ) : Finset (Fin m → Finset C) := by\n  classical exact (covers s).filter (fun S => (coverInstance S).mospValue ≤ k)\n\ntheorem mem_coversOfMospValueLe {s : Fin m → ℕ} {k : ℕ} {S : Fin m → Finset C} :\n    S ∈ coversOfMospValueLe s k ↔ S ∈ covers s ∧ (coverInstance S).mospValue ≤ k := by\n  simp [coversOfMospValueLe]\n\n/-- With at least one pattern and no empty pattern, some customer requires some\npattern in every cover, the hypothesis of `mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`. -/\ntheorem exists_requires_of_mem_covers {s : Fin m → ℕ} (hm : 0 < m) (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j)\n    {S : Fin m → Finset C} (hS : S ∈ covers s) :\n    ∃ c p, (coverInstance S).requires c p := by\n  have hcard : 0 < (S ⟨0, hm⟩).card := by\n    rw [mem_covers.1 hS ⟨0, hm⟩]\n    exact hs _\n  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Finset.card_pos.1 hcard\n  exact ⟨c, ⟨0, hm⟩, hc⟩\n\n/-- `mospValue ≤ k + 1` and `pathwidth ≤ k` cut out the same covers, by Yanasse's\nequality, when `m ≥ 1` and every pattern is nonempty. -/\ntheorem coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe {s : Fin m → ℕ} (hm : 0 < m)\n    (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j) (k : ℕ) :\n    coversOfMospValueLe (C := C) s (k + 1) = coversOfPathwidthLe s k := by\n  ext S\n  rw [mem_coversOfMospValueLe, mem_coversOfPathwidthLe]\n  constructor\n  · rintro ⟨hS, h⟩\n    refine ⟨hS, ?_⟩\n    rw [(coverInstance S).mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one\n      (exists_requires_of_mem_covers hm hs hS)] at h\n    exact Nat.le_of_add_le_add_right h\n  · rintro ⟨hS, h⟩\n    refine ⟨hS, ?_⟩\n    rw [(coverInstance S).mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one\n      (exists_requires_of_mem_covers hm hs hS)]\n    exact Nat.add_le_add_right h 1\n\n/-- **The first-moment count, MOSP reading.** With `m ≥ 1`, every `s j ≥ 1` and\n`k < n = |C|`, `t = (n − k + 1) / 2`,\n`#{S ∈ covers s : mospValue (coverInstance S) ≤ k + 1} ≤\n  n.choose t · (n − t).choose (t − 1) · ∏_j avoidCount n t (t − 1) (s j)`. -/\ntheorem card_coversOfMospValueLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (hm : 0 < m) (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j)\n    (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    (coversOfMospValueLe (C := C) s (k + 1)).card ≤\n      (Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) *\n        ∏ j, avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) := by\n  rw [coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe hm hs]\n  exact card_coversOfPathwidthLe_le s k hk\n\n/-- **The first-moment bound, MOSP reading**, over `ℝ`: the probability that a\nuniformly random cover of size vector `s` has MOSP value at most `k + 1`. -/\ntheorem prob_coversOfMospValueLe_le (s : Fin m → ℕ) (hm : 0 < m) (hs : ∀ j, 1 ≤ s j)\n    (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card C) :\n    ((coversOfMospValueLe (C := C) s (k + 1)).card : ℝ) /\n        ∏ j, ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ) ≤\n      (((Fintype.card C).choose ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2) *\n        (Fintype.card C - (Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2).choose\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) : ℕ) : ℝ) *\n        ∏ j, ((avoidCount (Fintype.card C) ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2)\n          ((Fintype.card C - k + 1) / 2 - 1) (s j) : ℝ) /\n            ((Fintype.card C).choose (s j) : ℝ)) := by\n  rw [coversOfMospValueLe_eq_coversOfPathwidthLe hm hs]\n  exact prob_coversOfPathwidthLe_le s k hk\n\nend MOSPFormalization","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01A99hqbGVu53dbHZgvKuyHR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
