s checked, 0 failures, 30","+new lines in `paper1/axiom_check.lean`). What is *not* in Lean, with the","+obstacle named: Lemmas P, G, F and Corollary S′ in component form (components","+of `G − S` as finsets with their sizes, §10.3), Theorem Cl's independence","+step (a product-over-blocks lemma for weighted sums over edge subsets), Lemma","+J and Theorem Cl-cover (inclusion–exclusion over pattern sets), the converse","+of L1′ (c). The paper may cite Theorem S as **proved in Lean** (finite form,","+inner probability as a weighted count), Theorem Cl as \"union bound and","+characterisation in Lean, independence step on paper\", Corollary W-flip as","+\"sound part in Lean, evaluation on paper\". Kill criterion: none (\"blocked","+with the obstacle\" was a deliverable; nothing is blocked that the item","+expected to be proved).","+","+### 10.1 What is proved, statement by statement","+","+All over `{V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]`, `n = Fintype.card V`,","+`t = (n − k + 1) / 2`, `r = (n − k) / 2` in `ℕ` arithmetic (so `t + r = n − k`","+and `r = n − k − t`, the item's form); `IsEmptyPair`, `gnpWeight`,","+`graphsOfPathwidthLe`, `edges` from `FirstMoment.lean`, `closedNbhd` from","+`EmptyPair.lean`, `coverGraph`, `coverInstance` from `CliqueCoverMoment.lean`.","+","+| §8.4 / §2.6 target | Lean name | status | rests on |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| L1 | `exists_balanced_separator`: `pathwidth G ≤ k → k < n → ∃ A R S, Disjoint A R ∧ Disjoint A S ∧ Disjoint R S ∧ A ∪ R ∪ S = univ ∧ A.card = t ∧ R.card = r ∧ S.card = k ∧ IsEmptyPair G A R` | **proved** | `exists_layout_vertexSep_eq_pathwidth` (new: the infimum is attained), `exists_empty_pair_of_layout` at `i = t − 1`, `Finset.exists_subset_card_eq` |","+| L3 (b), the cover form | `exists_balanced_separator_cover`: a cover with `mospValue ≤ k + 1` and some requirement, `k < n`, has the same `A, R, T` with `∀ j, Disjoint (S j) A ∨ Disjoint (S j) R` | **proved** | `mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`, `isEmptyPair_coverGraph_iff` |","+| `IsBalancedBip G S k` (pair form of `E_bip(S)`) | `∃ A R, Disjoint A R ∧ A ∪ R = univ \\ S ∧ A.card = t ∧ R.card = r ∧ IsEmptyPair G A R` | defined | — |","+| L1′ (a) | `exists_isBalancedBip`: `∃ S, S.card = k ∧ IsBalancedBip G S k` | **proved** | L1 |","+| the connectivity step | `mem_side_of_walk`, `componentOff_subset_side`: with `A ∪ R = univ \\ S` and `(A, R)` empty, every walk of `G` avoiding `S` that starts in `A` ends in `A`; `componentOff G S v ⊆ A` for `v ∈ A` | **proved** | induction on `SimpleGraph.Walk` |","+| L1′ (b) | `card_componentOff_le_of_isBalancedBip`: `IsBalancedBip G S k → v ∉ S → (componentOff G S v).card ≤ t` | **proved** | the row above; `componentOff G S v` is `univ.filter (ReachableOff G S v ·)`, `ReachableOff` = a walk whose support avoids `S` |","+| L1′ (d) | `not_isBalancedBip_threeK2` (`¬ IsBalancedBip threeK2 ∅ 0`) and `card_componentOff_threeK2_le` (every component of `3K₂ − ∅` has `≤ 3` vertices) | **proved** | `threeK2_no_balanced` by `decide +kernel` over the 64 subsets; `threeK2_walk_support` (a walk stays in `{u, partner u}`) |","+| L1′ (c), converse (component form ⇒ pair form) | — | **not formalised** | components as finsets, §10.3 |","+| the Galois step | `subset_compl_closedNbhd_iff`: `R ⊆ univ \\ closedNbhd G A ↔ Disjoint A R ∧ IsEmptyPair G A R` | **proved** | `mem_closedNbhd_iff`, `G.adj_symm` |","+| the monotone step | `closedNbhd_mono` | **proved** | — |","+| `IsClosedPair G A R` | `A = univ \\ closedNbhd G R ∧ R = univ \\ closedNbhd G A` | defined | — |","+| `closeStep G (A, R)` | `(univ \\ N[univ \\ N[A]], univ \\ N[A])`, one round, `A` first | defined | — |","+| L2 (i) | `subset_closeStep`: for an empty pair, `A ⊆ A*`, `R ⊆ R*` | **proved** | the Galois step twice (`subset_compl_closedNbhd_compl_closedNbhd`: `A ⊆ V ∖ N[V ∖ N[A]]` for *every* `A`) |","+| L2 (ii)–(iii) | `closeStep_isClosedPair`: `IsClosedPair G (closeStep G P).1 (closeStep G P).2` for **every** `P` | **proved** | Galois and monotone steps |","+| L2 (iii), the fixpoint | `closeStep_closeStep`: `closeStep G (closeStep G P) = closeStep G P` | **proved** | the row above; no iteration, no termination argument |","+| L2 (iv) | `sdiff_eq_inter_boundary_of_isClosedPair`: `univ \\ (A ∪ R) = (N[A] \\ A) ∩ (N[R] \\ R)` | **proved** | `mem_closedNbhd_iff` |","+| L2 (v) | `card_closeStep`: `t ≤ |A|`, `r ≤ |R|`, `|V ∖ (A ∪ R)| ≤ k` carry to the closure | **proved** | (i), `card_le_card` |","+| L1 + L2 | `exists_closedPair_of_pathwidth_le`: `pathwidth G ≤ k → k < n → ∃ A R, IsClosedPair G A R ∧ IsEmptyPair G A R ∧ t ≤ A.card ∧ r ≤ R.card ∧ (univ \\ (A ∪ R)).card ≤ k` | **proved** | L1, (ii), (v) |","+| characterisation step of Cl | `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both`: `IsClosedPair G A R ↔ Disjoint A R ∧ IsEmptyPair G A R ∧ ∀ v ∉ A, v ∉ R → (∃ a ∈ A, G.Adj a v) ∧ (∃ r ∈ R, G.Adj r v)` | **proved** | — |","+| Lemma W | `weightedCount_ge_indicator`: `(∀ P ∈ 𝓟, empty P → 1 ≤ Z P ∧ Z P ≤ (𝓟.filter empty).card) → (if ∃ P ∈ 𝓟, empty P then 1 else 0) ≤ ∑ P ∈ 𝓟, if empty P then 1 / Z P else 0` in `ℝ`; `one_le_weightedCount` | **proved** | `sum_le_sum`, `one_div_le_one_div_of_le`, `sum_filter` |","+| Lemma W, `G(n, p)` reading | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted`: for any `Z : SimpleGraph V → pairs → ℕ` admissible on every graph's empty pairs of `pairIndices t r`, `∑_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ ∑_G gnpWeight p G · ∑_{q ∈ pairIndices t r} (if IsEmptyPair G q.1 q.2 then 1 / Z G q else 0)` | **proved** | Lemma W, L1 (`exists_mem_pairIndices_isEmptyPair`); `pairIndices t r` generalises `emptyPairIndices` to exact sizes `(t, r)`, `card_pairIndices = n.choose t · (n − t).choose r` |","+| the union bound over separators | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_separators`: `∑_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ ∑_{S ∈ univ.powersetCard k} ∑_{G ∈ bipGraphs S k} gnpWeight p G` | **proved** | L1′ (a), `sum_biUnion_le_sum_of_nonneg` |","+| `isBalancedBip_induce` | `isBalancedBip_restrictOff`: `IsBalancedBip (restrictOff G S) S k ↔ IsBalancedBip G S k`, with `restrictOff G S` the graph of the edges of `G` off `S` (`Adj u v := G.Adj u v ∧ u ∉ S ∧ v ∉ S`) | **proved** | — |","+| `sum_gnpWeight_fiber` (the factorisation step) | for `H` with `restrictOff H S = H`: `∑_{G : restrictOff G S = H} gnpWeight p G = p^{|E(H)|} (1 − p)^{|pairsOff S| − |E(H)|}` | **proved** | the bijection `F ↦ fromEdgeSet (E(H) ∪ F)` from the subsets of `pairsMeeting S` onto the fibre (`sum_nbij'`), `edges_fromEdgeSet`, `sum_pow_mul_eq_add_pow` |","+| `card_pairsOff` | `|pairsOff S| = (n − |S|).choose 2` | **proved** | `pairsOff S` is the image of the edges of `⊤` on the subtype `↥(univ \\ S)` under `Sym2.map Subtype.val` (`pairsOff_eq_image`), `Sym2.map.injective`, `card_edges_top` |","+| the inner probability as a count on `V ∖ S` | `sum_gnpWeight_bipGraphs`: `∑_{G ∈ bipGraphs S k} gnpWeight p G = ∑_{H ∈ offGraphs S, IsBalancedBip H S k} p^{|E(H)|} (1 − p)^{|pairsOff S| − |E(H)|}`; `innerBip p S k` is that sum with `(n − |S|).choose 2` written out; `sum_gnpWeight_bipGraphs_eq_innerBip` | **proved** | `sum_fiberwise_of_maps_to` over `restrictOff · S`, the two rows above |","+| Theorem S, separator-summed | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_separator`: `∑_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ ∑_{S ∈ univ.powersetCard k} innerBip p S k` | **proved** | — |","+| the relabelling (the \"moreover\" of Theorem S) | `innerBip_eq_of_card_eq`: `S₀.card = S.card → innerBip p S₀ k = innerBip p S k` | **proved** | `exists_equiv_mem_iff` (a permutation of `V` carrying `S₀` onto `S`, from `Fintype.card_eq` on the subtypes and their complements and `Equiv.Set.sumCompl`); `relabel e G := G.comap e.symm`; `edges_relabel`, `card_edges_relabel`, `restrictOff_relabel`, `isBalancedBip_relabel_iff`; `sum_nbij'` |","+| **Theorem S** | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_choose_mul_innerBip`: for `0 ≤ p ≤ 1`, `k < n`, any `S₀` with `S₀.card = k`: `∑_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ (n.choose k : ℝ) · innerBip p S₀ k` | **proved** | the two rows above, `card_powersetCard` |","+| Theorem Cl, union bound | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs`: `∑_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ ∑_{q ∈ closedIndices t r} ∑_{G ∈ closedPairGraphs q.1 q.2} gnpWeight p G`, `closedIndices t r` the disjoint ordered pairs with `t ≤ |A|`, `r ≤ |R|` | **proved** | L1 + L2 |","+| Theorem Cl, independence step | `∑_{G : IsClosedPair G A R} gnpWeight p G = (1 − p)^{ar} ((1 − (1 − p)^a)(1 − (1 − p)^r))^s` | **not formalised** | the product-over-blocks lemma, §10.3 |","+| Lemma Fl | `isolatedIn G A`; `flipPair_isEmptyPair` (the four cases), `flipPair_disjoint`, `card_flipPair` (sizes preserved when `|J| = |J′|`), `flipPair_injOn` (`(J, J′) = (R* ∩ A, A* ∩ R)`), `flips G A R` (the image), `one_le_card_flips`, `card_flips_le` (the flips of an empty pair of `pairIndices t r` are distinct empty pairs of `pairIndices t r`, so `#flips ≤ X`) | **proved** | — |","+| Lemma Fl, the count `C(|I_A| + |I_R|, |I_A|)` | — | **not formalised** (not needed for admissibility; Vandermonde `Nat.add_choose_eq` would do it) | — |","+| Corollary W-flip, sound part | `weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_flipWeighted`: `∑_{pw G ≤ k} gnpWeight p G ≤ ∑_G gnpWeight p G · ∑_{q ∈ pairIndices t r} (if IsEmptyPair G q.1 q.2 then 1 / #flips G q.1 q.2 else 0)` | **proved** | Lemma W's reading, Lemma Fl |","+| Lemma J, Theorem Cl-cover, the evaluation of W-flip | — | **not formalised** | inclusion–exclusion over pattern sets, §10.3 |","+| Lemmas P, G, F; Corollary S′ | — | **not formalised** | components as finsets, §10.3 |","+| Propositions T, T-cover | — | not Lean targets | asymptotic and conditional on a cited LDP |","+","+The headline statement, verbatim from the file:","+","+```lean","+theorem weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_choose_mul_innerBip (p : ℝ) (hp0 : 0 ≤ p)","+    (hp1 : p ≤ 1) (k : ℕ) (hk : k < Fintype.card V) (S₀ : Finset V) (hS₀ : S₀.card = k) :","+    ∑ G ∈ graphsOfPathwidthLe (V := V) k, gnpWeight p G ≤","+      ((Fintype.card V).choose k : ℝ) * innerBip p S₀ k","+```","+","+with","+","+```lean","+noncomputable def innerBip (p : ℝ) (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ) : ℝ :=","+  ∑ H ∈ (offGraphs S).filter (fun H => IsBalancedBip H S k),","+    p ^ (edges H).card * (1 - p) ^ ((Fintype.card V - S.card).choose 2 - (edges H).card)","+```","+","+`offGraphs S` being the graphs on `V` with no edge meeting `S` — the graphs","+on `V ∖ S` kept on the vertex set `V`, as §8.4 recommended, which avoids a","+subtype vertex set everywhere except in the one count `card_pairsOff`. So","+`innerBip p S k` is literally `P_N(E_bip(t))` of Theorem S: the sum over","+the labelled graphs on `N = n − k` vertices in the pair-form event of","+`p^{|E|} (1 − p)^{C(N, 2) − |E|}`. Its value is what §5 computes by the","+partition formula (Lemma P), on paper; the Lean statement does not evaluate","+it, as the item's \"does not claim\" says.","+","+### 10.2 Beyond the brief","+","+The brief expected (a)–(c) and allowed (d) to be left as a named `Prop`.","+Everything in (d) was proved, and five further statements:","+","+1. **The relabelling.** §8.2 proves \"the inner probability does not depend","+   on `S`\" by the bijection graphs(V) ≅ graphs(V ∖ S) × 𝒫(pairs meeting S)","+   and a relabelling of `V`; the brief left it on paper. In Lean the","+   relabelling is `relabel e G := G.comap e.symm` for a permutation `e`","+   carrying `S₀` onto `S`, which exists whenever `|S₀| = |S|`","+   (`exists_equiv_mem_iff`, from `Fintype.card_eq` on `↥S₀ ≃ ↥S` and on the","+   complements, glued by `Equiv.Set.sumCompl`). Four invariances carry it:","+   `edges_relabel` (the edge set is mapped by `Sym2.map e`, so its size is","+   kept), `restrictOff_relabel` (restriction commutes with relabelling),","+   `isBalancedBip_relabel_iff` (the pair form is invariant, sides mapped by","+   `Finset.map`), and `sum_nbij'` with `relabel e.symm` as the inverse. This","+   turns the separator-summed form into Theorem S's `n.choose k · P_N(E_bip)`.","+2. **Theorem Cl's union bound** over `closedIndices t r`, from","+   `exists_closedPair_of_pathwidth_le`.","+3. **Lemma Fl** and the sound part of **Corollary W-flip**, so that the","+   weighted count with the flip weight is a theorem in Lean; what is on","+   paper is the *evaluation* of `E[Y]` by Lemma J.","+4. **L1′ (b)** as a theorem rather than a `Prop`, by defining the component","+   of `v` in `G − S` as the vertices reachable by a walk avoiding `S`","+   (`ReachableOff`, `componentOff`) instead of through Mathlib's","+   `ConnectedComponent` quotient; the connectivity step is an induction on","+   `SimpleGraph.Walk`.","+5. **L1′ (d)**, the `3K₂` example, both halves: `decide +kernel` over the","+   64 subsets for \"no `3`-set is an empty pair with its complement\"","+   (`threeK2_no_balanced`), and a walk lemma for the relaxed half.","+","+### 10.3 The obstacles, named","+","+* **Components as finsets** (Lemmas P, G, F; Corollary S′ in component","+  form; the converse of L1′ (c)). Lemma P sums over the integer partitions of","+  `N` and needs \"the components of `H` have sizes `λ`\" as a predicate on","+  graphs, with the count of set partitions of a given type and the","+  independence of the induced graphs on the blocks; Lemma G needs the fibre","+  \"the component of `v` is exactly `B`\" as `H[B]` connected ∧ no `B`–`Bᶜ`","+  edge; Lemma F needs both. None of this is in the development (Mathlib's","+  `ConnectedComponent.supp` is a `Set`, and connectedness of an induced","+  subgraph as a finset predicate is not there), and §8.4 priced it at more","+  than a session. **Not on Theorem S's path**, as §8.4 predicted: Theorem S","+  is proved with the inner probability defined as the weighted count of the","+  pair-form event. The converse of L1′ (c) (grouping components into two","+  sides of sizes `t`, `r`) is the same obstacle; the direction Theorem S","+  needs (pair form ⇒ every component inside one side) is proved.","+* **The product-over-blocks lemma** (Theorem Cl's independence step). The","+  closed-pair event is a conjunction of `1 + 2|S|` events on pairwise","+  disjoint blocks of pairs (no `A`–`R` edge; for each `v ∈ S`, some `A`–`v`","+  edge and some `R`–`v` edge), and its weighted count is the product of the","+  per-block counts times `1` for the free pairs. The general lemma — for a","+  family of disjoint blocks `B_i ⊆ edges ⊤` and predicates `P_i`,","+  `∑_{F ⊆ T, ∀ i, P_i (F ∩ B_i)} p^{|F|} (1 − p)^{|T| − |F|} = ∏_i ∑_{F_i ⊆ B_i, P_i F_i} p^{|F_i|} (1 − p)^{|B_i| − |F_i|}`","+  — is the fibre argument of `sum_gnpWeight_fiber` iterated over an index","+  type, with `Finset.prod_univ_sum` and a bijection `𝒫(T) ≅ piFinset (𝒫 ∘ B) × 𝒫(T ∖ ⋃ B)`;","+  estimated at a session on its own, and the only thing between Theorem Cl","+  and Lean. The characterisation step and the union bound are proved.","+* **Inclusion–exclusion over pattern sets** (Lemma J, Theorem Cl-cover):","+  `card_filter_avoid`'s pattern extended to the three cases of `allowed`","+  and the two-variable Möbius inversion; §8.4 said \"not within a session\",","+  and it was not attempted.","+","+### 10.4 The checks","+","+* **State before you prove.** Every statement above was checked before it","+  was written: L1, L1′, L2 on every graph to 9 vertices (§2.4), the","+  factorisation per `S`, Lemma W, Fl on every labelled graph to 6–7 vertices","+  in exact rationals (§8.3). Two statements are *stronger* than the checked","+  ones and were re-checked here: `closeStep_isClosedPair` and","+  `closeStep_closeStep` hold for **every** `A` (not only an empty pair), and","+  `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both` — both on every labelled graph to 5 vertices","+  and every `A` (and every disjoint `R`), `tests/test_separator_moment.py`","+  (`test_close_step_transcription_equals_close_pair`,","+  `test_sees_both_is_the_closed_pair_characterisation`).","+* **The numerical pin** (`python -m learning.sandwich --stage separator`,","+  1 s; `reports/scratch/separator_moment/10_lean/sandwich_separator.{md,log}`):","+  `learning/sandwich.py` transcribes `closeStep` (`close_step`) and the","+  right-hand side of `isClosedPair_iff_sees_both` (`sees_both`) literally,","+  and `separator_check` runs L1, L1′ (a)–(b), L2 (i)–(v), the","+  characterisation and the index-set memberships on **500 random","+  `G(n, p)` graphs at `n = 5–11` with exact pathwidth, at `k = pw` and","+  `k = pw + 1`: 1,000 rows, zero violations**, with `close_step` equal to","+  item 03's `close_pair(…, \"A\")` on every exact-size pair. `SEPARATOR_PROVED`","+  (30 names) joins `ALL_PROVED`, so `--stage lean` audits the new theorems","+  with the rest (`test_lean_theorems_are_sorry_free`).","+* **Axioms**: `make -C paper1/latex axioms` — 296 theorems checked, 0","+  failures (`10_lean/axiom_check.log`); the 30 new `#print axioms` lines are","+  under \"loop0011 item 10\" in `paper1/axiom_check.lean`. `lake build`:","+  `10_lean/lake_build.log`.","+* **Tests**: 5 new in `tests/test_separator_moment.py` (87 in the module):","+  the audited names are theorems of the file and the file has no `sorry`","+  and no `axiom`; the two transcriptions on every labelled graph to 5","+  vertices; `separator_check` on 60 graphs; the `3K₂` example.","+","+### 10.5 Where the record corrects the item","+","+* **No termination argument.** The item asked for the closure \"iterated;","+  termination by `|V ∖ (A ∪ R)|` strictly decreasing until the fixpoint\".","+  L2 (iii) says the closure is a fixpoint after one round, and the Lean","+  statement is stronger still: `closeStep` is idempotent on **every** pair,","+  empty or not (`closeStep_closeStep`), because `A ⊆ V ∖ N[V ∖ N[A]]` holds","+  for every `A` (`subset_compl_closedNbhd_compl_closedNbhd`). Emptiness is","+  needed only for monotonicity in `R` (`subset_closeStep`).","+* **The pair form suffices for Theorem S**, as §8.4 said; `IsBalancedBip` is","+  the pair form, and the component form appears only in L1′ (b).","+* **`|R| = n − k − t` is written `(n − k) / 2`**, equal in `ℕ` arithmetic","+  (`omega`); the item's expression is the same number.","+* **(d) fitted**, against the item's expectation, and so did the","+  relabelling the item did not ask for; the named `Prop`","+  `SeparatorFactorisation` was not needed.","+* **`decide` cannot do `IsBalancedBip` directly**: over `64 × 64` pairs of","+  subsets it hits the recursion limit; reducing to the 64 subsets `A`","+  (`R = univ \\ A` is forced) and `decide +kernel` settles it in under a","+  second. `native_decide` was not used (it would add an axiom).","+* **`componentOff` is not Mathlib's `ConnectedComponent`**: it is the","+  reachable set through walks avoiding `S`, as a `Finset` under classical","+  decidability. The two agree (a walk in `G.induce (V ∖ S)` is a walk of `G`","+  avoiding `S`), but the equivalence is not proved here and nothing rests","+  on it.","+","+### 10.6 Appendix A rows, drafted for item 12 (not in the paper)","+","+```latex","+\\leanentry{separator}{Appendix~\\ref{app:random}, counting events: a layout of width $k<n$ forces pairwise disjoint $A,R,S$ covering $V$ with $|A|=\\lceil(n-k)/2\\rceil$, $|R|=\\lfloor(n-k)/2\\rfloor$, $|S|=k$ and no $A$--$R$ edge (on the MOSP graph: no pattern meets both $A$ and $R$); a walk avoiding $S$ that starts in $A$ stays in $A$, so every component of $G-S$ has at most $\\lceil(n-k)/2\\rceil$ vertices; $3K_2$ at $k=0$ satisfies the component condition and not the bipartition one} \\leannames{exists_balanced_separator, exists_balanced_separator_cover, exists_isBalancedBip, card_componentOff_le_of_isBalancedBip, not_isBalancedBip_threeK2, card_componentOff_threeK2_le} \\\\","+\\leanentry{closedpair}{The closed pair: $R\\subseteq V\\setminus N[A]$ iff $(A,R)$ is disjoint and empty (the Galois step); one round of the alternating closure $R^{*}=V\\setminus N[A]$, $A^{*}=V\\setminus N[R^{*}]$ is monotone on empty pairs, lands on a closed pair ($A^{*}=V\\setminus N[R^{*}]$, $R^{*}=V\\setminus N[A^{*}]$) from every $A$, is idempotent, has separator $N(A^{*})\\cap N(R^{*})$ and keeps the sizes; a pair is closed iff it is empty and every outside vertex sees both sides; a layout of width $k<n$ forces a closed empty pair with sides of at least the forced sizes} \\leannames{subset_compl_closedNbhd_iff, subset_closeStep, closeStep_isClosedPair, closeStep_closeStep, sdiff_eq_inter_boundary_of_isClosedPair, card_closeStep, isClosedPair_iff_sees_both, exists_closedPair_of_pathwidth_le} \\\\","+\\leanentry{weightedcount}{Lemma~W: for any weight $1\\le Z(P)\\le\\#\\{\\text{empty pairs}\\}$ on the empty pairs, $\\sum_P \\mathbf 1[P\\ \\text{empty}]/Z(P)\\ge\\mathbf 1[\\text{some pair is empty}]$, so $\\Pr[\\pw\\le k]\\le E[\\sum_P \\mathbf 1[P\\ \\text{empty}]/Z(G,P)]$ over the exact-size pairs; with $Z$ the number of flips of $P$ (exchanging equally many vertices isolated in $G[A]$ and $G[R]$ gives distinct empty pairs of the same sizes), the weighted count of Corollary~W-flip} \\leannames{weightedCount_ge_indicator, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_weighted, flipPair_isEmptyPair, flipPair_injOn, card_flipPair, card_flips_le, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_flipWeighted} \\\\","+\\leanentry{theoremS}{Theorem~S, the separator first moment in finite form: for $0\\le p\\le1$ and $k<n$, $\\Pr[\\pw(G(n,p))\\le k]\\le\\binom nk\\,P_N(E_{\\mathrm{bip}})$, where $P_N(E_{\\mathrm{bip}})$ is the $G(N,p)$-weighted count, $N=n-k$, of the graphs on $V\\setminus S$ whose vertices split into an empty pair of sizes $\\lceil N/2\\rceil$, $\\lfloor N/2\\rfloor$; the union bound over the $\\binom nk$ separators is the only inequality: the graphs on $V$ with a given restriction to $V\\setminus S$ have total weight equal to the restriction's $G(N,p)$ weight (the pairs meeting $S$ carry weight $(p+(1-p))^{|\\text{pairs meeting }S|}=1$), and the inner count is the same for every $S$ by a relabelling of $V$} \\leannames{weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_choose_mul_innerBip, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_separator, weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_separators, sum_gnpWeight_fiber, sum_gnpWeight_bipGraphs, card_pairsOff, innerBip_eq_of_card_eq} \\\\","+\\leanentry{theoremCl}{Theorem~Cl, the union bound: $\\Pr[\\pw\\le k]\\le\\sum_{(A,R)}\\Pr[(A,R)\\ \\text{is closed}]$ over the ordered disjoint pairs with $|A|\\ge\\lceil(n-k)/2\\rceil$, $|R|\\ge\\lfloor(n-k)/2\\rfloor$; the evaluation of each term as $(1-p)^{|A||R|}\\bigl((1-(1-p)^{|A|})(1-(1-p)^{|R|})\\bigr)^{|S|}$ is on paper} \\leannames{weightedSum_graphsOfPathwidthLe_le_sum_closedPairs} \\\\","+```","+","+Item 12 should also add `SeparatorMoment.lean` to the file list in the","+comment at the head of `sec9e_appendix_random.tex`, and say in Appendix E","+that Theorem S is a Lean theorem and Theorem Cl's independence step is not.","+","+### 10.7 Regenerate, size range, kill verdict, what this does not claim","+","+* **Regenerate.** `cd lean && lake build` (the file builds in about 1.5 s","+  on a built library); `make -C paper1/latex axioms`;","+  `python -m learning.sandwich --stage separator` (1 s; add","+  `--out <path>` to keep `reports/sandwich_tables.md` as the full run","+  writes it) and `--stage lean` (the axiom audit through the sandwich","+  path); `python3 -m pytest tests/test_separator_moment.py -k \"proved_names or close_step or sees_both or separator_check or three_k2\"`.","+  Logs: `reports/scratch/separator_moment/10_lean/` (`lake_build.log`,","+  `axiom_check.log`, `sandwich_separator.{md,log}`, `gate.log`).","+* **Size range.** The theorems are for every finite `V`, every `k < n`,","+  every `0 ≤ p ≤ 1` (Lean, no size). The numerical pin: 500 random graphs at","+  `n = 5–11`; the transcription tests: every labelled graph to 5 vertices.","+* **Kill verdict: none** (the item had none). Nothing left as a `Prop`;","+  three groups of statements left on paper with their obstacles named in","+  §10.3.","+* **Does not claim.** Any value or rate of `P_N(E_bip)`: `innerBip` is a","+  finite weighted sum, evaluated on paper by Lemma P (§5) and never in Lean.","+  That Theorem Cl is in Lean: its union bound and characterisation step are,","+  its independence step is not. That Corollary W-flip's right-hand side is","+  evaluated: only `P ≤ E[Y]` with the flip weight is proved. That","+  `componentOff` equals Mathlib's connected component (not proved, not","+  used). That Lemma Fl's count is `C(|I_A| + |I_R|, |I_A|)`: only `1 ≤ #flips ≤ X`","+  is proved, which is all admissibility needs. Nothing probabilistic beyond","+  finite weighted counts; Propositions T and T-cover stay on paper with","+  their hypotheses. Nothing re-solved; `solutions/` untouched."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/separator_moment.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012CQAStg2R4eD5m1fxY4o5m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
